          "question": "e-291",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The tangent line approximation to $f(x)$ at the point $a=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{\u2032}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(-2)+{f}^{\u2032}(-2)(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =0+2(x+2) \\\\  & =2(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-1.8)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=-1.8.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1.8) & \u2248L(-1.8) \\\\  & =2(-1.8+2) \\\\  & =2(0.2) \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
