          "value": "The tangent line approximation to $g(x)$ at the point $a=4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =g(a)+{g}^{\u2032}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =g(4)+{g}^{\u2032}(4)(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $g(4)=3,$ and since $g'(x)=\\sqrt{x},$ then $g'(4)=\\sqrt{4}=2.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =3+2(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $g(3.6)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=3.6.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3.6) & \u2248L(3.6) \\\\  & =3+2(3.6-4) \\\\  & =3+2(-0.4) \\\\  & =3-0.8 \\\\  & =2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
